Comparing our Week 2 inventory (21 items) with the industry systems showed that we had covered the core product, account, cart and order data but were missing data that customers rely on to make and trust a purchase. The main new data items were size and colour variants, size guides, reviews and ratings, estimated delivery date, shipping cost, return and refund policy, promo codes, order history and tracking number with courier. For the front end, each of these needs a place in the interface: a size and colour selector and size guide on the product page, delivery and returns information near the price, promo code entry in the cart, and an order history and tracking view for logged-in customers. Our risk analysis showed that price, stock and cart total need server-side validation, so the front end will display these values but never be the source of truth. For the Week 4 database design, we will add tables or fields for variants, reviews, promo_codes, order_history and tracking_number. Admin-only data such as revenue and customer lists will be protected with role-based access control. Best-selling products and low-stock alerts were identified as useful dashboard reports.
